---
// One synthetic patient as an HL7 v2 PID segment and as the FHIR R4 Patient it maps to.
// The numbered names follow Synthea's convention, so the record reads as synthetic at a glance.
---

<figure class="mapping">
	<div class="panel">
		<p class="label">HL7 v2 PID segment</p>
		{/* The wbr tags let a narrow screen wrap between fields instead of inside a value. */}
		<pre><code>PID|<wbr />1|<wbr />|<wbr /><mark class="f1">100234^^^GEN^MR</mark>|<wbr />|<wbr /><mark class="f2">Rivera954^Ana972^M</mark>|<wbr />|<wbr /><mark class="f3">19740312</mark>|<wbr /><mark class="f4">F</mark>|<wbr />…</code></pre>
	</div>
	<div class="panel fhir">
		<p class="label">FHIR R4 Patient</p>
		<pre><code>{`{
  "resourceType": "Patient",
`}<span class="identifier">{`  "identifier": [{
    "type": { "text": "MR" },
    "value": `}<mark class="f1">"100234"</mark>{`
  }],
`}</span>{`  "name": [{
    "family": `}<mark class="f2">"Rivera954"</mark>{`,
    "given": [`}<mark class="f2">"Ana972"</mark>{`, `}<mark class="f2">"M"</mark>{`]
  }],
  "birthDate": `}<mark class="f3">"1974-03-12"</mark>{`,
  "gender": `}<mark class="f4">"female"</mark>{`
}`}</code></pre>
	</div>
	<figcaption>
		<ul class="legend">
			<li><span class="key f1">PID-3</span> identifier</li>
			<li><span class="key f2">PID-5</span> name</li>
			<li><span class="key f3">PID-7</span> birthDate, reformatted</li>
			<li><span class="key f4">PID-8</span> gender, F mapped to female</li>
		</ul>
		<p>A synthetic patient. The mapping standard decides each conversion, such as the date format and the gender code.</p>
	</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
	.mapping {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.panel {
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
	}
	.fhir {
		margin-left: 2rem;
	}
	.label {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
	}
	pre {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		border: 0;
		background: none;
		overflow: visible;
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		white-space: pre-wrap;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	mark {
		color: inherit;
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 0 0.125rem;
		box-decoration-break: clone;
		-webkit-box-decoration-break: clone;
	}
	.f1 {
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--field-1) var(--field-alpha), transparent);
		box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--field-1);
	}
	.f2 {
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--field-2) var(--field-alpha), transparent);
		box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--field-2);
	}
	.f3 {
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--field-3) var(--field-alpha), transparent);
		box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--field-3);
	}
	.f4 {
		background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--field-4) var(--field-alpha), transparent);
		box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--field-4);
	}
	figcaption {
		margin-left: 2rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
	}
	.legend {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
		padding: 0;
		color: var(--secondary);
	}
	.key {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-right: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0 0.25rem;
		border-radius: 4px;
		color: var(--text);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
	}
	figcaption p {
		margin: 0;
	}
	@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
		.panel {
			box-shadow: none;
		}
	}
	/* On phones the figure keeps three mappings and drops the identifier and the legend, so the projects stay close. */
	@media (max-width: 30rem) {
		.fhir,
		figcaption {
			margin-left: 0;
		}
		.identifier,
		.legend {
			display: none;
		}
		pre mark.f1 {
			background: none;
			box-shadow: none;
		}
	}
</style>
